{
  "country": "DE",
  "description": "Months (1-12) transcribed cell by cell from the BZfE chart 'Der Saisonkalender' (all rows of its Gemüse and Obst sections, nothing added). Per the chart legend ('Erklärung'), plain yellow bars are imports (tall = 'Monat mit starken Importen', low = 'Monat mit geringen Importen') and hatched bars are domestic production ('Monat mit großem Angebot aus heimischem Anbau'; hatched over yellow = 'großes Angebot aus heimischem Anbau und gleichzeitig geringen Importen'). 'months' = every month with any hatched (domestic) bar, including months the bar covers only partly (several bars start or end mid-month). The hatched bars are drawn in steps of a quarter of the row height; the lowest step is a thin band, which the legend does not label. 'peak' = months whose hatched bar is taller than that thin lowest band, read as big domestic supply; months with only the thin band are in 'months' but not in 'peak'. Items with no hatched month are imports only ('domestic': false, empty 'months'). The chart does not distinguish fresh from stored produce, so no item has 'storage'. Items not listed are not on the chart.",
